# Digests contemper's own buildimg (hack/volumes-support/buildimg at contemper
# commit f2b07bd81cf63ceaac064a99afc76fd2498742a5) produced for the files in
# volumes-support/, pushed with -tag v1 to a local registry at localhost:5555 under
# the prefix localhost:5555/contemper-e2e. Regenerate by starting a registry on
# localhost:5555, checking out that contemper commit and running, from its root:
#   go run ./hack/volumes-support/buildimg -prefix localhost:5555/contemper-e2e \
#     -tag v1 -support-dir <this directory> [-revision <sha>] -digests-file out.txt
# (the support-dir is volumes-support/ here, without image.json). The base image's
# digest depends on the prefix, because its annotations name the variants by digest
# under it. The first block was run without -revision, the second with
# -revision 0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567.
